{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SECOND, DISTINCT FLAKE observed on the same Gerrit change (1640) — recording here so both live in one place. This one is NOT the maintenance.lock race; it is a different test on a different platform, which is why the 'one hot flake' theory was dropped.\n\nTEST: tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::test_plan_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union\nOBSERVED: CI run 31575183167, leg 'pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.12)'. 1 failed, 152 passed.\nSIGNATURE: AssertionError: clones do not share a base\n\nMECHANISM: the failing line is a FIXTURE PRECONDITION, not the property under test. In _assert_emit_is_append_only:\n\n    for _ in range(retain):\n        assert emit(repo_a, ticket_id) is True\n    _git('push', '-q', 'origin', 'HEAD:tickets', cwd=tracker_a)\n    _expire_sync_marker(tracker_b)\n    _engine_run(repo_b, 'list')                                    # <- clone B is expected to pull here\n    base_a = _sidecar_paths(tracker_a, ticket_id, event_type)\n    assert len(base_a) == retain, 'base padding did not reach the bound'\n    assert base_a == _sidecar_paths(tracker_b, ticket_id, event_type), 'clones do not share a base'   # line 1702\n\nClone B is driven to sync by expiring its sync marker and running an engine command whose pull is incidental to the assertion. When that pull does not land A's pushed sidecar events, the test fails while establishing its own setup — the append-only/reconvergence behaviour it exists to prove is never actually exercised. So a red here is not evidence of a product defect.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX: make the sync an explicit, asserted step rather than a side effect of _engine_run(repo_b, 'list') — e.g. fetch/merge directly in the fixture and assert the expected sidecar set is present before proceeding, or retry the sync until it converges with a bounded timeout. Failing the setup should be reported distinctly from failing the invariant.\n\nSHARED CONTEXT: both flakes cost change 1640 a Verified -1 (runs 31571454820 and 31575183167). Both pass locally, including on a base rebased to current origin/main. Neither test is on the ACLI-auth code path that change touches. Neither is deterministic.\n\nConsider widening this ticket to 'de-flake the two CI scaffolding races' or splitting the sidecar one out — they share a root shape (test setup depending on unasserted timing) but not a fix."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786522915458923001,"uuid":"11e0c1bc-a142-4684-92d6-6f97f71da8bd"}